\par
In terms of resources, the cost of implementing the CA in its first year was
\par
approximately US \$40 million. Of this, nearly one-quarter (the largest
\par
apportionment) of the budget was designated for LC operations. On the one
\par
hand, this may be interpreted as recognition by the international community
\par
of the importance of logistics in humanitarian operations. Alternatively, it
\par
may be an indicator of the decades of neglect that logistics has experienced
\par
in the humanitarian realm.
\par
Business as usual or\dots{} ?
\par
As noted above, the gaps identified by the HRR in logistics relate mainly to
\par
coordination and capacity deficiencies, both of which are important
\par
dimensions in facilitating effective disaster management. The gaps included
\par
a lack of inter-agency contingency planning; the absence of a global network
\par
of warehouse facilities for use in rapid response to emergencies; lack of
\par
supply-chain information exchange (no coordinating body exists) or
\par
communications platforms for such exchanges between IGOs, NGOs,
\par
donors, suppliers; no global mapping of inventory of relief stocks; lack of
\par
inter-agency logistics response teams (LRTs) to carry out comprehensive
\par
and timely needs assessments; a strong need for improved information
\par
exchange on use of military and civil defense assets (MCDA) as part of
\par
emergency/humanitarian response; and a lack of coordination of airfield
\par
traffic and congestion during emergencies and especially natural disasters
\par
(OCHA, 2006a).
\par
As the LC lead, WFP has demonstrated consistent and strong leadership
\par
and coordination. For example, it dedicates staff to focus on information
\par
and mapping logistics data as part of the inter-agency contingency planning
\par
process. WFP maintains its capacity to provide sufficient, high-quality
\par
supplies for preparedness and response and coordination with other actors
\par
of pre-positioning of relief inventories and warehousing arrangements (eg
\par
via its five Humanitarian Response Depots). It also identifies urgently
