The Value of Perfect Information
\par
The goal is to build a single index related to a
\par
segment or a set of segments that prospectively (i.e.,
\par
on expectation before drilling any segments) is able
\par
to help us formulate a drilling strategy. We are in-
\par
terested in building an a priori exploration time-
\par
table no matter the result of possible exploration
\par
wells. This would be a useful tool for oil and gas
\par
companies because the planned drilling strategy has
\par
to be submitted in advance, along with the number
\par
of trial segments. The definition of VoPI in this
\par
context is strongly affected by the choice of the
\par
strategy that the company wants to pursue. By the
\par
word strategy, we mean both the exploration part
\par
and the subsequent development strategy. As dis-
\par
1434 Bayesian Networks for Prospect Analysis in the North Sea
\par
cussed in the previous section, we introduce some
\par
simplifications to handle this problem, but many
\par
possible solutions still exist, depending both on the
\par
personal choice of the decision maker and on the
\par
actual sequence of events. The intrinsic difficulty
\par
of integration of risk analysis with production strat-
\par
egy definition has been effectively underscored in
\par
Suslick and Schiozer (2004, p. 4), where the au-
\par
thors point out that``several alternatives are pos-
\par
sible, and restrictions have to be considered.''
\par
The basic ideas of our strategy can be resumed
\par
