\par
environmental conditions and time-specific management actions.
\par
A policy At expresses state-specific actions to be taken at each
\par
point in time, starting at time t and extending over the remain-
\par
der of the timeframe. For notational convenience we assume in
\par
what follows that there are only finitely many states, so that the
\par
system state can be represented with counting indices. We begin
\par
with a description of optimal decision making on assumption that
\par
resource dynamics are fully known and understood. Then we allow
\par
