\par
On reflection this is expected; the 2 expected values of partial
\par
information are constructed with the conditional distributions qk\textbar k{$\prime$}
\par
and qk{$\prime\vert$}k, whereas the expected value of perfect information is con-
\par
structed with a joint distribution over both uncertainty factors.
\par
Unless k and k{$\prime$} are independent, the partial distributions do not
\par
