We begin in Section 2 by formalizing the policy problem
\par
we are considering and writing down the decision tree. In
\par
Section 3, we introduce the computer model for the system
\par
and describe the ways in which it can be used to generate
\par
the probabilities on our decision tree. In Section 4,
\par
we introduce our Sequential Emulation algorithm for
\par
mimicking a backwards induction in order to visualize our
\par
expected loss surface as a function of policy. In Section 5,
\par
we illustrate our methods using an example of a CO2
\par
abatement policy. We suggest some methods of policy
\par
support using the results of the Sequential Emulation in
\par
Section 6. We offer discussion in Section 7.
