\par
influence that a former SEC employee might have on a matter.
\par
Representatives from law firms, including some with former SEC
\par
employees, stated that any useful information former SEC employees
\par
take with them when they separate from SEC likely would be of little value
\par
by the time current cooling-off periods expire. Some SEC employees with
\par
whom we spoke also stated that extending cooling-off periods would
\par
