\textbf{2. Instances Where Recusal Is Required}
\par
a) \emph{Recusal from Examinations and Inspections Based Upon Borrowing Relationship/Seeking Credit.}
\par
1. \emph{Recusal required. }An examiner may not examine any entity, or an affiliate of any entity,
\par
from which the examiner or the examiner's spouse or dependent child, or a related entity,
\par
7
\par
is borrowing, leasing, or seeking credit.
\par
7 A ``related entity'' means an entity in which the examiner, the examiner's spouse or dependent child owns or
\par
controls more than ten percent of its equity, or a partnership in which the examiner or his or her spouse is a
\par
general partner.
\par
-37-2. \emph{Exceptions:}
\par
a) An examiner may examine any entity, including any affiliate of such entity, from
\par
which the examiner, the examiner's spouse or dependent child has obtained a
\par
credit card in accordance with paragraph 1 (B) (2) (a) above.
\par
b) An examiner may examine the affiliate of any entity from which the examiner, the
\par
examiner's spouse or dependent child:
\par
i. Has a loan secured by residential real property in accordance with
\par
paragraph 1 (B) (2) (a) above.
\par
ii. Has an overdraft protection line.
\par
iii Is borrowing against the cash value of a life insurance policy.
\par
The credit card, loan secured by residential real property, overdraft protection line, or
\par
insurance policy loan must not have been provided on terms more favorable than
\par
those available to the public.
\par
\emph{Example}
\par
An examiner has an overdraft protection line on his checking account at a national bank subsidiary
\par
of a bank holding company. The examiner may examine any affiliate of the national bank, including
\par
the parent bank holding company. However, as pointed out in paragraph 2 (A) (1) of this Part, the
\par
examiner may not examine the national bank.
\par
Another example is borrowing against the cash value of a life insurance policy issued by an
\par
insurance subsidiary of a financial holding company. The examiner may participate in an
\par
examination or inspection of an affiliate that is supervised by the Federal Reserve.
\par
3. \emph{Servicing relationships. }An examiner may participate in an examination of, or a
\par
supervisory matter involving, an organization that services a loan of the employee or the
\par
employee's spouse or dependent child, unless the examiner knows the servicer has
\par
retained a financial interest in the underlying value of the credit.
\par
4. \emph{Waiver. }In limited circumstances, the examiner's supervising officer, in consultation with
\par
the Bank's Ethics Officer, may provide written authorization for an examiner to examine
\par
an institution, or an affiliate of an institution, with which the examiner, his or her spouse,
\par
dependent child or a related entity has a borrowing relationship, although participation in
\par
the examination otherwise would be prohibited under paragraph 2 (A) (1) above.
