-38-b) \emph{Recusal from Supervisory Matters (Other Than Examination/Inspection) Based on Borrowing}
\par
\emph{Relationship.}
\par
\emph{1 Recusal requirement. }An examiner may not participate in any supervisory matter involving
\par
an institution or any affiliate if the examiner, or the examiner's spouse or dependent child,
\par
or a related entity, is indebted to the institution or any affiliate.
\par
\emph{2 Exceptions.}
\par
a) Recusal is not required if the debt was not extended on terms more favorable than
\par
those available to the public, all payments are current, and the debt is extended
\par
through:
\par
i) A line of credit extended through a credit card.
\par
ii) An amortizing consumer credit loan (including a first or second mortgage
\par
on a personal residence) or a home equity line of credit.
\par
iii) An overdraft protection line.
\par
iv) A student loan.
\par
v) A car lease.
\par
vi) A loan against the cash value of an insurance policy.
\par
b) In addition, recusal is not required with respect to any debt of the examiner's
\par
spouse or dependent child, or a related entity of the spouse or dependent child if:
\par
i) The debt is the sole responsibility of the spouse, child or related entity, and
\par
is not derived from the examiner's income, assets or activities.
\par
ii) The examiner has no knowledge of the identity of the lender.
\par
\emph{Example}
\par
The following illustrates how the recusal standards described in paragraphs 2 (A) and 2 (B) are
\par
based on the type of assignment, rather than if the person is credentialed.
\par
An examiner with a student loan from a national bank may not participate in an examination of the
\par
bank, its parent or any affiliate as such participation would violate System policy and could be a
\par
violation of criminal law. On the other hand, System policy allows the examiner to be assigned to
\par
handle a supervisory matter concerning the bank, the parent company or an affiliate, so long as
\par
payments on the student loan with the national bank are current, and it was obtained on terms not
\par
more favorable than those available to the public. If, instead, the examiner has a business loan with
\par
the bank, System policy requires that the examiner be restricted from handling any supervisory
\par
matter involving the bank, the parent company or an affiliate.
