-43-\textbf{PART II. RULES FOR OTHER EMPLOYEES WITH SUBSTANTIVE}
\par
\textbf{RESPONSIBILITIES RELATING TO SUPERVISION AND REGULATION MATTERS}
\par
These rules apply to the Bank President and other senior Bank officials who have responsibilities
\par
relating to supervision or regulation of financial institutions, all non-credentialed professional staff,
\par
including officers and managers, who participate substantially in supervisory matters (e.g., attorneys
\par
and certain economists), and all professional staff, including officers and managers, who participate
\par
in the discount window function. These persons are referred to as a "covered employee(s)".
\par
Supervisory matter does not include participating in an examination. See the introduction to this
\par
Appendix for examples of what this term does cover.
\par
\textbf{1. Prohibition Against Seeking Credit if Handling Supervisory Matter}
\par
A. \emph{General Prohibition. }A covered employee is generally not restricted from borrowing from any
\par
entity, including one for which the System is the primary supervisor. However, a covered employee
\par
may not, on his or her own behalf, or on behalf of anyone else, seek or accept a loan from, or renew
\par
or renegotiate a loan with, an institution or any affiliate if the covered employee is working on or
\par
knows he or she will be assigned a supervisory matter which involves the institution or any affiliate.
\par
Furthermore, a covered employee must disqualify himself or herself from handling a supervisory
\par
matter involving an institution or any affiliate if the covered employee learns that his or her spouse
\par
or dependent child or a related entity is seeking or has sought or accepted a loan from, or has
\par
renewed or renegotiated a loan with the institution or any affiliate while the matter is pending before
\par
the Bank or the Board.
\par
The foregoing prohibitions continue for three months after the covered employee's participation in
\par
the matter ends.
\par
B. \emph{Exceptions. }These prohibitions do not apply to a line of credit extended through a credit card, an
\par
overdraft protection plan, or a loan against the cash value of a life insurance policy that was
\par
obtained on terms not more favorable than those available to the public (i.e., the terms were not
\par
offered or enhanced because of the covered employee's position at the Bank).
\par
C. \emph{Waiver. }A written waiver from the prohibitions of this paragraph may, in some limited
\par
circumstances, be obtained from the covered employee's supervising officer, in consultation with the
\par
Bank's Ethics Officer.
\par
-44-\textbf{2. Recusal from Supervisory Matter Based Upon Borrowing Relationship}
\par
