\par
ii) An amortizing consumer loan (including a first or second mortgage on a personal
\par
residence) or a home equity line of credit.
\par
iii) An overdraft protection line.
\par
iv) A student loan.
\par
v) A car lease.
\par
vi) A loan against the cash value of an insurance policy.
\par
2. Recusal is not required with respect to any debt of the covered employee's spouse or
\par
dependent child, or a related entity of the spouse or child if:
\par
i) The debt is the sole responsibility of the spouse, child or related entity, and is not
\par
derived from the covered employee's income, assets or activities.
\par
ii) The covered employee has no knowledge of the identity of the lender.
