E. \emph{Waiver. }In certain cases, the prohibitions contained in paragraphs 3 (A) and 3 (C) may be waived
\par
by the covered employee's supervising officer, in consultation with the Bank's Ethics Officer.
\par
-46-\textbf{APPENDIX C}
\par
\textbf{Responsibilities of the Ethics Officer}
\par
1. The Ethics Officer, a senior officer of the Bank reporting to the President and First Vice
\par
President, is responsible for implementing the Bank's program for maintaining the highest standards
\par
of honesty, integrity, and impartiality in the conduct of the Bank's activities. The Ethics Officer is
\par
available to employees and officers alike.
\par
2. The Ethics Officer annually distributes the Code to all officers and employees.
\par
3. The Ethics Officer annually distributes a financial disclosure form to all officers and to employees
\par
with supervisory, procurement, or policymaking responsibilities.
\par
4. An employee or officer may consult, orally or in writing, with the Ethics Officer about the
\par
application of the Code in a particular situation. The Ethics Officer provides counsel and guidance
\par
to the employee or officer about the conduct that the Ethics Officer considers appropriate under the
\par
Code. An officer or employee may also raise questions with his or her supervising officer, a Human
\par
Resources officer, the General Counsel, the First Vice President, or the President.
\par
5. The Ethics Officer shall consult with the Bank's General Counsel, as appropriate, about matters
\par
involving interpretations of the Code or the application of statutes and regulations to Bank staff.
\par
6. The Ethics Officer may file in the confidential files of the Ethics Office a succinct report on
\par
guidance given to an employee or officer. From time-to-time the Ethics Officer may release to the
\par
entire Bank staff compilations of guidance given to employees of officers after deleting all
\par
information identifying the particular employee or officer.
\par
7. The Ethics Officer may from time-to-time prepare educational material about the Bank's ethics
\par
program and distribute it to the entire Bank staff or to areas that would find that information helpful.
\par
8. The Ethics Officer consults with the President and First Vice President about broad issues
\par
concerning the Bank's ethics program and may recommend revisions to policies or new areas to be
\par
covered by policies.
\par
9. The Ethics Officer has such additional responsibilities with regard to the Bank's ethics program
\par
as the President or First Vice President may specify.
\par
10. The President or First Vice President may appoint Deputies to the Ethics Officer as appropriate.
