\par
The subgroup analysis showed bendamustine to be cost-effec-
\par
tive across a heterogeneous patient group. In each of the sub-
\par
groups analyzed, the ICER remained below \pounds 14,000 per QALY.
\par
Figure 6 shows the results of the probabilistic sensitivity anal-
\par
ysis as distributions of simulations on the cost-effectiveness plane
\par
and as a cost-effectiveness acceptability curve. At the \pounds 20,000 per
\par
QALY threshold, the probability of bendamustine being cost-effec-
\par
tive is 90\%. The expected value of information associated with the
\par
decision problem is \pounds 403. Based on a 10-year stream of 1079 cases
\par
per annum, the EVPI is estimated at \pounds 3.7 million at a willingness-
\par
to-pay threshold of \pounds 20,000 per QALY and \pounds 0.8 million at a thresh-
\par
old of \pounds 30,000 per QALY.
