\par
Expert commentary \& five-year view
\par
Over the past two decades, HTA in Canada has evolved and
\par
grown rapidly, which establishes Canada as an international leader
\par
in this field. With the lessons learned and experience accumu-
\par
lated, HTA has matured to be an important tool in aiding clinical
\par
practice and policy-making at national, regional and institutional
\par
levels across the country. This article provides a high-level sum-
\par
mary of the current state of HTA in supporting decision-making
\par
in Ontario and Canada. We focused on those initiatives in which
\par
the authors have been directly and extensively involved to illus-
\par
trate an example of collaboration between academic researchers
\par
and decision makers in Canada. Therefore, it might not repre-
\par
sent HTA initiatives in other jurisdictions. Based on the authors'
\par
knowledge and experience, some research expectations were
\par
highlighted that might potentially take place in the next few years
\par
(e.g., prioritization, evidence synthesis and MCDA).
