3.2.1. Fuzzy simulation results
\par
The remediation period is set to 2 years for the various reme-
\par
diation alternatives. Through fuzzy simulation, the distributions of
\par
the benzene concentration at the study site under various scenar-
\par
ios could be obtained. In this study, one simulation run on a 3 GB
\par
RAM and 1.86 GHz Duo-Core PC took about 30 s. As the fuzzy vertex
\par
method required many rounds of simulation, the total simulation
\par
time was about 1 h. Fig. 5 presents the most likely distributions for
\par
the plume contamination (i.e. when the membership degree is 1)
\par
for the six remediation scenarios.
\par
In general, the results in Fig. 5 show that the concerned reme-
\par
