environmental standards into their business policies to maintain competitiveness.
\par
A new management research area, so-called closed-loop supply chain (CLSC),
\par
has evolved to assist companies in recognizing potential benefits and overcom-
\par
ing challenges associated with its operations and strategies. The CLSC concerns
\par
the integration of material flows, financial flows, and information flows through-
\par
out both forward chain and reverse chain. It reflects a generalization and extension
\par
of traditional supply chain concepts. The CLSC, especially the reverse logistics
\par
system with the third-party reverse logistics providers (3PRLP) is very impor-
\par
tant for materials recycling, resources saving, and environment protecting activ-
\par
ities. Several companies in many countries have started recognizing the strategic
\par
value of integrating environmental principles into business policies and have devel-
\par
oped innovative product recovery programs to recover and reuse their end-of-life
\par
products.
\par
In China, with reference to the experience of developed countries in environmen-
\par
tal protection and effective pollution control, the State Environmental Protection
\par
Administration of China launched a program called ``Creating Environment-
\par
Friendly Enterprises''. More recently, the National People's Congress pointed out
\par
that it's vital to speed up to enhance development of recycling economics, especially
\par
to excogitate a new generation of recycled steel-making processes which incorpo-
\par
rate products manufacturing, energy saving, and social wastes reusing together
\par
in order to improve environmentally-friendly operations. Even the steel and iron
\par
scrap has become an essential material in steel manufacturing or/and remanufac-
\par
turing process. At present, the popular recycling mode in Chinese steel industry
\par
is directly collecting scraps by manufacturers and for their own remanufacturing
\par
process. It may increase purchase costs, prolong remanufacturing cycles, and stunt
\par
sustainable development. How to establish specialized scrap bases locally and how
\par
to make full use of professional skills of the 3PRLP have been the urgent problems
\par
in Chinese steel industry. This steel scrap recycling mode based on 3PRLP can
\par
not only decrease purchasing risks and investment and enhance the scrap qualities
\par
and remanufacturing equipments availability, but also can improve environmentally
\par
friendly operations.
\par
As we have illustrated above, remanufacturing, recycling, and reusing are becom-
\par
ing increasingly popular because of growing consumer awareness, legislative initia-
\par
tives, and profitability of the recovery business. Based upon the practices of Chinese
\par
steel manufacturing industry, our research goal is three-fold. First, considering the
\par
impacts of environmental legislation on scraps recycling, we established the multi-
\par
echelon CLSC system framework based on the third-party reverse logistics. Second,
\par
we analyze the closed-form analytic expressions for both united optimization strate-
\par
gies in integrated closed-loop system and the one-leader-multiple-follower Stackel-
\par
berg strategies in decentralized system. We also make comparisons between them
\par
to identify the condition of closed-loop system being coordinated. Lastly, combin-
\par
ing with the practical operations of scrap supply chain in Chinese steel industry,
\par
we carry out some simulation experiments to gain an insight into the impacts of
