7. Conclusions
\par
In this research, we investigated the strategic value of
\par
information sharing within a marketing channel consisting
\par
of one manufacturer, one dominant retailer and two identical
\par
small retailers. Our intention is to explore the optimal
\par
decisions regarding the choice of channel member for
\par
information sharing to best benefit of the manufacturer. We
\par
first derived pricing strategies and the resulting profits under
\par
five different information scenarios:
\par
1 non-information sharing between the channel members;
\par
2 manufacturer engages in information sharing with the
\par
dominant retailer exclusively;
\par
3 manufacturer engages in information sharing with one of
\par
the small retailers exclusively;
\par
4 manufacturer engages in information sharing with both
\par
the dominant retailer and one of the small retailers
\par
simultaneously; and
