\emph{2.3 Initialisation with data and simulation}
\par
This sub-section initialises the sample model described in the previous section with data
\par
to represent a realistic problem. Sample data initialisation includes few steps as shown in
\par
Figure 1. To solve the optimisation problem with the initialised data, IpOpt algorithm is
\par
used. The IpOpt algorithm implements an interior point line search filter method that
\par
aims to find a local solution of the objective function subject to constraints. The
\par
mathematical details of the algorithm are in various publications (Waechter, 2002;
\par
Waechter and Biegler, 2005a, 2005b, 2006; Nocedal et al., 2005). The algorithm is
\par
intended to solve non-linear problems; however, it is also capable of providing solutions
\par
for various other types of problems as well as linear problems.
