\par
significant differences in the 30-day rates of major bleeding
\par
or the composite endpoint of cardiac death, MI, or stroke
\par
(10). However, all patients in this trial received a 300-mg
\par
loading dose of aspirin, which may have diminished the
\par
ability for differences to emerge given the short follow-up
\par
duration. In light of these conflicting results, the recent
\par
2011 consensus guidelines for PCI give a new class IIa
\par
recommendation, that it is reasonable to use 81 mg/day
\par
maintenance aspirin dose instead of higher doses (18).
\par
In the present study, there were numerous differences in
\par
