\par
Conclusions
\par
In the current study, we found no difference in ischemic
\par
endpoints between high- and low-dose aspirin used in
\par
combination with clopidogrel, but high-dose aspirin was an
\par
independent predictor for higher rates of major bleeding.
\par
Thus, absent a demonstrated benefit of high-dose aspirin in
\par
patients on dual antiplatelet therapy with clopidogrel fol-
\par
lowing PCI, and given the concern of potential harm of
\par
high-dose aspirin used with more potent P2Y12 inhibitors
\par
(i.e., prasugrel and ticagrelor), these data support the rou-
\par
tine use of low-dose aspirin ( 200 mg daily) at discharge
\par
following primary PCI in STEMI.
