Appendix. Measurement scale and items
\par
Information quality (INF) (adapted from Kim et al. (2004))
\par
INF1: Mobile banking provides me with information relevant to my needs.
\par
INF2: Mobile banking provides me with sufficient information.
\par
INF3: Mobile banking provides me with accurate information.
\par
INF4: Mobile banking provides me with up-to-date information.
\par
System quality (SYS) (adapted from Kim et al. (2004))
\par
SYS1: Mobile banking quickly loads all the text and graphics.
\par
SYS2: Mobile banking is easy to use.
\par
SYS3: Mobile banking is easy to navigate.
\par
SYS4: Mobile banking is visually attractive.
\par
Structural assurance (SA) (adapted from McKnight et al. (2002a))
\par
SA1: I feel confident that encryption and other technological advances on the mobile Internet
\par
make it safe for me to use mobile banking.
\par
SA2: I feel assured that legal and technological structures adequately protect me from payment
\par
problems on the mobile Internet.
\par
SA3: Mobile Internet is a robust and safe environment in which to use mobile banking.
\par
Trust propensity (PRO) (adapted from Koufaris and Hampton-Sosa (2004))
\par
PRO1: It is easy for me to trust a person/thing.
\par
PRO2: I tend to trust a person/thing, even though I have little knowledge of it.
\par
PRO3: My tendency to trust a person/thing is high.
\par
Initial trust (TRU) (adapted from Lee (2005))
\par
TRU1: Mobile banking is trustworthy.
\par
TRU2: Mobile banking keeps its promise.
\par
TRU3: Mobile banking keeps customers' interests in mind.
\par
Perceived usefulness (PU) (adapted from Agarwal and Karahanna (2000))
\par
PU1: Using mobile banking can improve my living and working performance.
\par
PU2: Using mobile banking can increase my living and working effectiveness.
\par
PU3: I find that mobile banking is useful.
\par
Usage intention (USE) (adapted from Lee (2005))
\par
USE1: Given the chance, I intend to use mobile banking.
\par
USE2: I expect my use of mobile banking to continue in future.
\par
USE3: I have intention to use mobile banking to conduct payment.
