4. Methodology
\par
4.1 Instrument development
\par
The research model includes seven factors. Each factor is measured with multiple items.
\par
All items are adapted from extant literature to improve content validity (Straub et al.,
\par
2004). These items were first translated into Chinese by a researcher. Then another
\par
researcher translated them back into English to ensure consistency. When the
\par
instrument was developed, it was tested among 12 users with rich LBS usage experience.
\par
Then according to their comments, we revised some items to improve the clarity and
\par
understandability. The final items and their sources are listed in Appendix 1. All items
\par
were measured with a seven-Likert scale, ranging from strongly disagree (1) to strongly
\par
agree (7).
\par
Items measuring four dimensions of privacy concern are adapted from Stewart and
\par
Segars (2002). Four items of collection reflect users' concern about the over-collection of
\par
their personal information. Items of improper access reflect users' concern about the
\par
unauthorized access to their personal information. Four items measuring errors reflect
\par
users' concern about information accuracy. Four items measuring secondary use
\par
reflect users' concern about information sharing and sale without their consent.
