Appendix 1. Measurement scales and items (SP means service provider)
\par
Collection (COL) (adapted from Stewart and Segars (2002))
\par
COL1: I feel bored when this SP asks me to provide personal information.
\par
COL2: I will think twice when this SP asks me to provide personal information.
\par
COL3: It bores me to provide personal information to so many people.
\par
COL4: I feel that this SP collects too much personal information about me.
\par
Improper access (IA) (adapted from Stewart and Segars (2002))
\par
IA1: This SP should invest more time and effort on preventing the unauthorized access to
\par
personal information.
\par
IA2: This SP should take more measures to ensure that unauthorized users cannot access
\par
personal information.
\par
IA3: The databases containing personal information should be protected from
\par
unauthorized access, no matter how much it costs.
\par
Errors (ERR) (adapted from Stewart and Segars (2002))
\par
ERR1: Personal information in the databases should be double checked to ensure its
\par
accuracy, no matter how much it costs.
\par
ERR2: This SP needs better procedures to correct the errors in personal information.
\par
ERR3: This SP should invest more time and effort on verifying the personal information in
\par
databases.
\par
ERR4: This SP should take more measures to ensure the accuracy of personal information.Secondary use (SU) (adapted from Stewart and Segars (2002))
